Bundle-Name: Fennec Services RSA Example API
Bundle-Description: \
	The interface, and nothing else — the one bundle a provider and a \
	consumer of the example share. That is the ordinary OSGi shape, and \
	the reason an import can load the class at all.

# The interface says who may call it with the Jakarta security
# annotations (Ledger). They are read from the class at export, so the
# package has to be there at runtime — from 2.1, which is what the
# Jersey 3.1 launches carry; the buildpath brings 3.0.
-buildpath: \
	jakarta.annotation-api;version=latest

Import-Package: \
	jakarta.annotation.security;version="[2.1,4)",\
	*
